The '''Liga Progressivo''' was a pro-business and pro-[[Volisania]] political current in mid-nineteenth-century Sarta. It drew support from coastal merchants, company directors, export interests, and other groups that benefited from trade and industrial growth.

The league favoured closer commercial ties with Volisania, a weaker system of labour protections, and continued reliance on the royal companies that managed major sectors of the economy. Its strongest base lay in the capital and the coastal cities, where industrial expansion and shipping made stability attractive to business elites.

== Political position ==

Liga Progressivo politicians argued that Sarta should preserve economic cooperation with Volisania while pursuing gradual institutional change. They were generally more willing than their rivals to tolerate worker discipline, company control, and the existing dominance of the lords' parliament.

The league became one of the two main political divisions of the era, opposing the anti-Volisania and pro-worker [[Union del Personajes]].

== Base of support ==

Its supporters were strongest in [[Bahia Alta]], [[Mariapolis]], and the commercial districts tied to the royal companies. The league's politics reflected the interests of ports, exporters, and state-linked business families.

